 "notes": [
  "PROPOSED (Gilfoyle 2026-10-23, Build 20) — not yet reviewed by Sparky. Edit in tools/perfboard.html, Export JSON, commit to docs/boards/coil_driver.layout.json.",
  "Board: plated-through, double-sided perfboard (cd_board; Sparky 05:35). Solid wires = top side, dashed = bottom side. A wire is soldered at every hole it bends at (each vertex), nowhere else.",
  "Coil paths (drains, sources, star, 12 V − return, +12 V feeds) in 18–20 AWG solid core, not thin jumper wire (Sparky 05:35). Gate/signal wires 22 AWG (PROPOSED).",
  "STAR ground at hole V22: the three FET sources, the 10k pull-downs, Teensy A signal GND (J-SIG.1) and the single 12 V − return (J-GND.2 -> TB-GND) all land there and nowhere else.",
  "Gate: Teensy pin -> 100 Ω -> G; 10k G-to-S on the FET side of the 100 Ω (PINMAP S01–S03; chief review #10).",
  "FETs stand upright, pins G-D-S left to right (IRLB8721PbF datasheet p.1). No heatsink (Sparky 05:35, guide check #6).",
  "Logic/signal terminals on the bottom edge, coil terminals on the top edge (guide §2, Sparky 05:35/05:36).",
  "OPEN for Sparky: the F-COIL 12 V input (J-12V) is fed from the e-stop NC block outputs (E02 BLK1 -> both EV200 coil +, E03 BLK2 -> AEV14012 coil +), never raw F-COIL, so the e-stop still cuts coil + (PROPOSED). The guide (step 10) currently keeps coil + OFF the board; if Sparky keeps that, delete J-12V and the three COIL+ pins.",
  "OPEN for Sparky: guide step 9 says Teensy A signal GND already lands at TB-GND (G04). J-SIG.1 joins it at this board's star as asked; wiring BOTH is a second ground path (loop). Fit only one (UNVERIFIED).",
  "Strain relief: tie every off-board lead down next to its terminal; never let a solder joint hold a wire. 4× M3 standoffs at the corner holes; sealed box (Sparky 05:35).",
  "Flyback: D-PRE 1N4007 is OFF-BOARD, across the AEV14012 coil terminals (DECIDED Sparky 05:41). No diode on either EV200: built-in economizer (SOURCED, TE datasheet)."
 ],
